{
  "id": "olfactory-bulb",
  "term": "olfactory bulb",
  "definition": "The olfactory bulb is an egg-shaped structure on the cribriform plate of the ethmoid bone where the olfactory nerve ends. It contains nerve cells, including mitral cells, and is a site where smell-related nerve signals connect in olfactory glomeruli; the term also includes the accessory olfactory bulb that receives input from the vomeronasal organ.",
